cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Magnetide: a zero-dependency analytic screen model for a benchtop MHD conduction pump"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tang
    given-names: Reynard Filbert
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lo20xl/magnetide"
abstract: >-
  A pure-Python-stdlib analytic model and parametric sweep harness for a
  benchtop magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) conduction pump driven by permanent
  magnets. Separates electrode length from axial field extent, applies a
  bubble-coverage correction to effective conductivity inside the integrator,
  and finds the operating point by bisection against the supply rail rather
  than by sweeping current. Includes buildability gates (magnet tilability,
  end-effect ratio, fuse limit, budget) and Blender-based verification of the
  generated STL geometry. Validated against one bench measurement of saline
  channel resistance: the model predicts 4.93 ohm against a measured 4.4 ohm,
  erring conservative.
keywords:
  - magnetohydrodynamics
  - mhd-pump
  - conduction-pump
  - seawater
  - permanent-magnet
  - analytic-model
  - parametric-optimization
  - blender-stl
